    {
     "collapsed": false,
     "id": "9f484e8b-405c-5198-873f-75e1c890c196",
     "gridsterCoords": {
      "w": 12,
      "x": 1,
      "h": 5,
      "y": 1
     },
     "state": "",
     "type": "TextDisplay",
     "title": "How to read this",
     "config": {
      "refreshInterval": 300,
      "widgetId": "9f484e8b-405c-5198-873f-75e1c890c196",
      "description": "",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "refreshContent": {
       "refreshContent": false
      },
      "customFilter": {
       "filter": [],
       "excludedResources": null,
       "includedResources": null
      },
      "selfProvider": {
       "selfProvider": true
      },
      "editorData": "<p style=\"color:#7f8c9a\"><b style=\"color:#9fb0c0;font-weight:bold\">Memory tiering sizing &mdash; sample.</b> Every tile below reads a metric the\nvCenter adapter already collects. <b style=\"color:#9fb0c0;font-weight:bold\">No super metrics are required for this dashboard</b>; if you\nimport <code style=\"color:#7f8c9a\">supermetric.json</code> as well, the derived figures become available for a second\nscreen.</p>\n<p style=\"color:#7f8c9a\"><b style=\"color:#9fb0c0;font-weight:bold\">This is a sizing tool, not a monitoring tool.</b> It answers <i style=\"color:#7f8c9a\">what hardware would this\nworkload need if it were tiered</i>. On a vSphere 8 estate there is no tiering to report, which\nis the point &mdash; the assessment happens before the upgrade.</p>\n<p style=\"color:#7f8c9a\"><b style=\"color:#9fb0c0;font-weight:bold\">Reading this on a cluster that already has tiering enabled?</b> Then\n<code style=\"color:#7f8c9a\">mem|host_provisioned</code> is <i style=\"color:#7f8c9a\">presented</i> memory &mdash; installed DRAM plus the NVMe\ntier &mdash; not installed DRAM. Measured on a tiered lab host: 639.4 GiB presented against a\n127.9 GiB DRAM tier, a 5.00&times; overstatement. Every tile labelled <i style=\"color:#7f8c9a\">presented memory</i>\nsays presented for that reason. On an untiered vSphere 8 host the two are the same number.</p>\n<p style=\"color:#7f8c9a\"><b style=\"color:#9fb0c0;font-weight:bold\">Tiles show the latest sample, not a peak.</b> Sizing must be done on business-cycle peaks,\nwhich need a View transformation rather than a dashboard tile. Treat these values as a shape\ncheck, not as the number on the quote.</p>",
      "locationFile": "",
      "locationUrl": "",
      "viewModeHTML": true
     },
     "height": 0,
     "tabId": "089a4b09-27fb-5213-9836-e9dd8f0e2639"
    },
